This file marks dev/fixtures/skins as a test fixture root. Skins.qml checks
for it before honoring QSG_SKIN_ROOT, so an accidentally-inherited env var
on a real deployment does nothing useful by itself: the production skins/
tree shipped in the package never contains this marker (dev/ is not part of
the installed derivation). This is an accident guard, not a security
boundary -- anyone able to set QSG_SKIN_ROOT on the greeter's actual process
already has enough access to plant this marker too. The real barrier
against arbitrary QML execution is the skin-name validation in Skins.qml.
